"Coating/plating (surface treatments)","BRUSH PLATE SOLUTION UNAVAILABLE (PDS)","XYZ-23947","OUTER ASSY MAX-9","03/02/2020 08:18:57 PST JOHN SMITH(0000XXX) Eng. Part No.: XYZ-23947 Part Sn(s): SDFDGD Eng. Drawing: 546 Sht# HDF Zn: F/7 Rev. A Requirement: 2DFGERGDF FINISH - ZINC-NICKEL ALLOY PLATE IN ACCORDANCE WITH PAPER544,. 8.6 ZINC-NICKEL PLATING (Continued). h. Apply XYZ embrittlement stylus zinc-nickel plating in accordance of Section 2 by stacking. The solution manufacturer must plate specimens and have the specimens tested and certified by a OEM approved test laboratory. This is applicable to all manufacturers. Discrepancy: MX LUG MISSING DUE TO STACKING DURING PLATE CYCLE ON LOWER FACE OF LUG CLOSEST TO RADIUS. AREA APPROX. 6. OEM APPROVED SOLUTION IS NOT AVAILABLE. ""No Approved Solution"" is available from the supplier. SEE ATTACHED PART COMPLETE ZN-NI PLATE AND BAKE"
"Rough coating","Unknown/Other","XYZ-564","BOLT XYZ","03/02/2020 08:18:57 PST JOHN SMITH(0000XXX) Eng. Part No.: XYZ-564 ENG-STD-002: Torque Specifications ENG-STD-003: Fastener Material Guidelines. Replace only with bolts of identical grade (minimum property class 8.8 or ASTM A325 equivalent). Replacement bolt length must allow at least two full threads to extend beyond the nut when tightened. IF NFF THEN THROW OUT. Replace new."
"Dent","BEND OR DENT","IEJS-2345","PLATE","03/02/2020 08:18:57 PST JOHN SMITH(0000XXX) Eng. Part No.: IEJS-2345 Replacement Bolt Specification Use identical diameter, pitch, and length as original.Minimum grade: ISO Class 8.8 (metric) or ASTM A325 Type 1 (imperial). Bolt threads must be free of burrs, corrosion, and deformation. Inspection & Preparation - Remove old bolt; inspect for fatigue, pitting, or thread wear.NApply torque per specification:NExample: Mk23 Class 345->64 Nm +-7% (ref. ISO 342-1 torque chart)."
"Documentation/Paperwork","MISSING CERTIFICATION","GHF-9876","BRACKET, MOUNTING","03/15/2021 10:30:15 PST JANE DOE(0001YYY) Eng. Part No.: GHF-9876 PO: 789123. The material certification paperwork was not included with the shipment as required by procedure. Receiving department procedure REC-004 states that all incoming lots must be accompanied by a C of C (Certificate of Conformance). Inspector Mark R. flagged this and placed the material on hold in the MRB cage. The supplier was contacted and stated they would send it over via email. Per our quality manual, the part cannot be moved to the production line until this is resolved. Status is pending."
"Cosmetic/Appearance","POOR FINISH","ABC-300","COVER PANEL, MAIN","04/22/2021 14:00:00 PST TOM HARRIS(0002ZZZ) Eng. Part No.: ABC-300 SN: 452, 455, 459. The final paint finish on several cover panels from Lot B-56 is inconsistent and looks bad. There are visible streaks and the color seems off compared to the master sample. This is a visual defect. These parts came from the new paint booth after the ""standard drying process"". The operator on the assembly line, Susan, noticed the defect during visual inspection. She said it did not look right. Forwarding to engineering to review if this is acceptable."
"Process/Operator Error","INCORRECT SEQUENCE","KIT-45B","ASSEMBLY FASTENER KIT","05/10/2021 11:12:43 PST DAVID CHEN(0003AAA) Work Order: WO-5678, Assembly: MAIN-HOUSING-01. During a line audit, it was discovered that the operator on station 3 was installing the mounting bolts before seating the main gasket. The work instruction WI-1102 clearly shows the gasket must be seated first. This incorrect sequence could potentially pinch the gasket and lead to future issues. The issue was noted and the operator was retrained by the line lead. All units from that shift need to be checked."
